{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1559565-advice-for-making-a-homebrew-family-of-dead","id":1559565,"title":"Advice for making a homebrew family of Dead?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-22T09:14:06-07:00","id":1559565,"title":"Advice for making a homebrew family of Dead?","content":"I've been wanting to make a family of the dead who get their powers and feed off of devotion and filial piety. I was thinking it would be two branches, one from the east and one of the manes of Rome, both attaching themself to families to protect them or help them out in exchange for worship and piety. <br /> <br /> My main idea came from the requiem for rome 2e book where a mortal woman recounts how when she lost her first child her father, a vampire pretending to be a mane, came and comforted her, and when she was behind on rent, he showed up once again to help her pay. <br /> <br /> I've got fluff down but I wanted advice on mechanics and how to make it balanced","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-10T05:03:54-07:00","id":1559869,"title":"","content":"If they were ghosts, I would have suggested modeling them off the idea of ancestral spirits that watch over their living descendants.<br /> <br /> Though as walking dead, I sadly have no idea what to do with them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T20:12:26-07:00","id":1559977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1559565-advice-for-making-a-homebrew-family-of-dead?p=1559869#post1559869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they were ghosts, I would have suggested modeling them off the idea of ancestral spirits that watch over their living descendants.<br /> <br /> Though as walking dead, I sadly have no idea what to do with them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Can't the dead inhabit buildings or just vibe as ghosts instead of directly using bodies? And yeah, ancestral spirits was what I was thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","user":"Snailslayer","date":". 05-14-2026, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T20:51:05-07:00","id":1559978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1559565-advice-for-making-a-homebrew-family-of-dead?p=1559977#post1559977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't the dead inhabit buildings or just vibe as ghosts instead of directly using bodies? And yeah, ancestral spirits was what I was thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the impression I got. But yeah, it was the most thematic option I could think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}